WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.980
It has been a while.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.610
Mother, it’s Kageto.
Is everybody doing well?

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.270
I am well.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:12.990
Right now, there are many newcomers
at the Pantasia store that I am working at.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.450
My juniors, Kawachi Kyousuke and Azuma Kazuma,

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.120
are doing well and have reached the semifinals.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:24.120
During this time, taking care of the Southern Tokyo Branch has been left entirely to me.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.130
But today, Manager, Azuma-kun,
Kawachi-kun, and Tsukino-san...

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.460
are all coming back.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.220
I’m really happy having everybody back.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.130
I’m really relieved.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:37.390
The big surprise this time was the hearts circling us.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.850
However, it really surprised me to find that
Katsuo and Manager are the same age.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.100
He’s twice as old as me!

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.940
Is that so?

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.650
But...

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.570
I wonder if the fact that I’m the only one working...

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.530
is all my imagination...

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.030
Welcome!

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.370
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.330
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.580
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.030
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:15.220
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:19.020
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:36.160
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:44.130
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:51.960
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:59.720
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:07.190
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:16.570
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:25.330
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:29.590
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.550
is the light of only you.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.330
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:41.140
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:48.860
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:52.810
The nightmarish semifinals!!

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.450
Yukino’s despicable trap!

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.030
Oh, yeah, Kawachi...

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:00.950
What?

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.540
I’ve been meaning to ask you for a while.
Is Old Man Kuroyanagi our senpai?

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.290
I’m only 22 years old!
I’m not an old man!

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:09.710
Yeah, of course.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.670
If we’re speaking of the order in which we joined Pantasia, Kuro-yan is way before us.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.250
So, he’s a senpai, in those terms.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.000
Oh, I see!

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:18.510
What about me...?

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.090
What about it...?

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.720
No, it’s just what Kanmuri said.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.220
He called Old Man Kuroyanagi, “Kuroyanagi-senpai.”

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.190
Kuroyanagi-senpai probably just can’t use his hands.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.940
It just struck me as odd then.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.660
Is that so?

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:38.440
Well, that may be so, but it’s probably for the reason that I was just talking about.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.150
Kuroyanagi-senpai...

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:42.700
I could never speak like that.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.120
I get it!

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.870
I’m beginning to see who Kanmuri really is.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.370
Who he really is?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:54.040
Kuroyanagi was put in charge of the
Main Store at the young age of 22.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.130
Do you know what
the trick behind that was?

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.670
Because he’s an excellent examiner?

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.630
Actually, he can probably make fantastic bread!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.720
That’s true... However,

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.600
in the mere three years after he joined,

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.640
the reason he managed to get to
the position he’s presently at is...

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:09.640
that he’s...

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.250
Ha...

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:13.640
Va...

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.900
Harvard University.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.900
It’s because he’s a graduate from
Harvard’s Food Sciences research program.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:21.820
Right, Manager?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.580
Kuro-yan’s a Harvard graduate?!

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.540
But, isn’t Harvard an elite amongst
the elite of America’s universities?!

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.380
You could never even imagine
this from his moronic reactions...

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.210
Ahh, annoying!

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.050
Not paper!

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:47.510
Melon!

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.430
Yakisoba...

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.570
Dog!

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:59.990
Kou... chin... mi...

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.880
The monster from outer space...

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.170
Is that true, Tsukino?

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.420
Yes, it is...

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.920
Please get the rest of the story from Manager.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.920
Is it true, Manager?

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.420
Listen up!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.720
This is an age of research being done even on bread.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.430
Chemical seasoning.
Flavoring. Preservatives.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.270
The creation of additives that are tasty,

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:36.190
yet 100% harmless for consumption,
is the dream of the bread industry.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.350
No!

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.400
It would not be wrong to call it
the dream of humanity as a whole!

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.400
That’s true...

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.320
That’s why once every few years,

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.780
even Pantasia hires students with an outstanding background in Food Science research.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:50.620
And this year,

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.080
there was a rumor that a newcomer even better than Kuroyanagi had been hired.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.290
And you think that’s Kanmuri?

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:58.790
Probably.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:03.300
Kuroyanagi was able to skip grades and
graduate from Harvard at the age of 19.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.800
But, it seems that this
particular newcomer graduated at age 16.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.550
Well, at least age-wise,
Kanmuri appears to be one level higher.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.020
I don’t know anything about him being a genius,

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.850
but if it comes to studying all
the time, I won’t be losing to him.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:18.270
That’s the way to go, Kawachi!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:19.900
I wonder...

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.490
Their research involves...

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.240
the study of something that is
most desired by the industry right now.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.280
Native yeast.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.000
Native yeast?

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:36.620
Native yeast is usually extracted
from raisins and apples,

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:39.460
but hundreds of varieties of yeast other than that exist.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.000
Ones which are able to transform
the taste of bread into infinite varieties.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.010
Unless you have many facilities and much knowledge,

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:50.600
you can’t isolate a special
yeast that produces a good taste.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:04.650
In other words, with the
monetary backing of Azusagawa Yukino,

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.900
if Kanmuri is able to isolate a special native yeast,

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.320
then Kawachi, you wouldn’t...

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.360
No, even I definitely can’t win.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.830
Kawachi?

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.460
That’s not funny!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:44.020
All the time that you don’t spend
baking bread is spent holed up here, isn’t it?

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.610
It makes me wonder
what you’re made of.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.780
The little ones here are delicate.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:51.120
If you don’t care for them properly, they die quickly.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.870
Please do not smoke in the laboratory.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.160
I believe that “No smoking” is written
in up to eight languages over there.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.710
However, yeast are ultimately germs, aren’t they?

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.340
Germs?!

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.710
To be treating these things
with such care...

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:13.680
I really don’t understand this “race” of bakers.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.850
So, are you done with what I asked of you?

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.350
The endo-proteases, right?

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:19.930
They’re done.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:20.890
Here you go.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.570
Well done.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:25.400
Endo-proteases,

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.570
hydrolytic enzymes
that can cleave proteins.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:30.490
As the name indicates,
it can digest proteins,

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:33.320
but what are you going to be using such a thing for?

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.450
Oh, that’s right,

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:37.870
you don’t like me asking any unnecessary questions.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:46.010
Keep quiet and do your work if you
want to continue to receive funding.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.380
There’s no learning curve with her, is there?

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.220
Oh well...

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:58.640
As long as I’m funded,

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:02.770
I need not get involved any
further with someone who dares

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:04.900
call my cute, little yeasts “germs.”

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.490
I’m sorry, Azuma.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:18.620
It doesn’t look like the finals will be
Southern Branch vs. Southern Branch.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:20.620
Kawachi...

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:23.210
Against the Shinjuku Central Branch...

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:26.120
Against Kanmuri... I can’t...

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.670
It’s too early to be giving up!

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:30.500
There has to be a way.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.050
If we try thinking about it
with all we have...

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.050
It’s easy to say that, but...

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:37.510
How can you be saying something so cowardly?

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:41.640
The two of you vowed to win at
Tsukino-san’s mother’s grave, didn’t you?

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:42.810
I’ll cooperate, too.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.060
Come on, now. Stand up.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.060
I wonder if I should put it
more aggressively?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:01.410
Something to help us win against the native yeast...

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.120
What can we do?

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.500
What can we...

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.000
What...?

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:17.470
This is hatsuga genmai yeast...

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.510
apparently.
Note: Hatsuga Genmai (<b>発芽玄米) means “germinated brown rice.”</b>

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:21.000
Hatsuga genmai yeast?!

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.560
This is the hatsuga genmai yeast

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:30.810
that Manager uses to make his ultimate,

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.520
delicious French bread?

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:36.990
This is actually an original,
native yeast made by Manager.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:41.450
Back then, he created this
without any facilities or money.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.580
That’s why Kuroyanagi really respects Manager.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.330
Please make me a student of yours!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:49.160
All right.
Please make me a student of yours!

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.590
With this, we might have a chance!

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:54.210
It’s too early to be celebrating.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:54.670
Huh?

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:58.050
Manager made this batch of yeast three years ago.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:01.980
As far as the fickle research community
is concerned, this is an ancient yeast.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:08.680
“Don’t forget that the enemy is still
leading, in terms of favorable conditions!”

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.190
That’s what he said.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:19.490
After having all this done for me,

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.990
if I were to lose now,
I’d be nothing more than a clown.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.200
Yup, a clown.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:27.040
Azuma, I’ll definitely win against Kanmuri.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.910
So, you win against Suwabara.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:29.790
Yeah.

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:30.660
Let’s win!

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:35.180
And let’s make our finals the best possible match.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:38.300
I really want to fight it out with you, Kawachi.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.840
We can do it, right?

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.880
Of course.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.900
Good luck, brats.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.520
Looks like you guys have finally figured it out.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.230
Come, I’ll cooperate, too.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:57.020
So let’s make it together.
A complete bread!

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.030
Hmm... is that a little too high and mighty?

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:05.290
It might be better to be a little friendlier...

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:09.000
If he slacks off any more than this,

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.040
he’s fired.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.220
What’s with this crowd of people?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.390
From the semifinals onward,

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:32.890
spectators aside from authorized
personnel are allowed to watch.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:36.770
In addition to regular folk, we have
gourmet critics and magazine journalists.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:40.400
Newspaper journalists and
various other people come, too.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.910
Wow... However, while it’s the semifinals,
it’s still a match amongst newcomers...

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:49.120
So much free time for... I mean, I
should be saying that Pantasia’s amazing.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.790
That’s true,

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:54.380
but most of them have probably really come for... him.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.640
Kirisaki, look over here!

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:07.970
Please remove the mask.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.850
It can’t really cover the
beauty that lies beneath, anyway.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:18.060
He’s a strange guy who appears
only during the newcomers’ battle.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.820
Meister Kirisaki that is...

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.860
Other than that, he doesn’t appear very much at all.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.200
Regardless of the reason for which they’ve come...

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:25.530
Customers are customers.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:29.950
Let’s show them our amazing skills,
and have all their gazes turn toward us!

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.250
Yeah!

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.660
Exactly, that’s how it should be.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.630
You seem to have found some
wonderful newcomers, haven’t you?

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.590
Let’s both do our best, shall we, Tsukino?

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.640
Stop!

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:52.140
Give me back my mother!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:58.560
Who’s that?

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:00.980
What’s wrong?

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.360
You’re not going to introduce your sister to them?

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.030
What a troublesome child you are.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.570
Stop it.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:10.170
Tsukino doesn’t like it.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.160
You’re Yukino-han, right?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.670
What? Yukino?

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:20.420
I don’t know what you’re trying to pull here,
but don’t be touching our Boss like that.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:21.210
Yeah!

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.710
I seem to be quite hated here...

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:27.520
But, I guess it can’t be helped...

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.510
Tsukino, I’m really sorry.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.010
Your onee-chan was really young then.

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.220
I couldn’t bring myself to acknowledge you then.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.900
But now... now...

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:41.660
Stop with the bad acting, Yukino.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:46.230
The Southern Tokyo Branch
has nothing to discuss with you.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.790
Ken-san... You, too?

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:53.080
But I guess it’s me who’s to blame.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:53.780
But...

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.710
But someday, I hope you can forgive me.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:00.420
Tsukino...?

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:06.930
I believe that such a day will come. Someday...

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:13.600
Is she really that Yukino?

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:14.680
I think so...

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:19.190
A true villain never really appears as one.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.650
It’s time,

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.570
but Dave Hashiguchi-sensei is not here yet.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:34.410
We plan to begin as soon as sensei arrives.

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.080
Okay.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:35.240
And...

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.080
Kuroyanagi-senpai.
And...

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:36.700
Kuroyanagi-senpai.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.210
Hello. It’s been a while, Kuroyanagi-senpai.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.330
Shigeru, eh?

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.340
And why are you here?

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.010
This is the assembly hall for the newcomers’ battle.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:49.670
I’m the examiner,
and you’re the newcomer,

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:51.600
so stop calling me senpai!

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:56.140
As time passes, people change, don’t they?

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:56.980
What?

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:58.680
At Harvard...

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:01.900
you loved me so much.

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.020
What?!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:03.900
Love...

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:08.900
Hey, stop making announcements
that invite misinterpretation!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.820
As you came to America at the age of 12,

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:14.660
I merely helped you out a little because
you were from Japan too!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.910
It was nothing more, and nothing less than that!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:19.580
Oh my, there’s no need
to get all worked up.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.660
It’ll just make it be taken all the more seriously, Examiner Kuroyanagi.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.790
But, more importantly, there was
something I wished to report.

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:30.840
In the three years after Senpai graduated...

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:33.300
I’ve finally completed... that.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:34.800
W-What?

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.930
You’ve completed it, you say?

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:40.270
I’d wanted to announce it earlier,

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:42.440
but I won by default every time, haven’t I?

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:45.230
But, it appears that I’ll have a proper match today.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.660
So look forward to it, okay?

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.200
Is something wrong?

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.030
No.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.200
Oh, that’s right.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.530
I had something to report to Kuroyanagi-kun as well.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:01.290
Yes.

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:08.540
Love is rather like the chaos found in outer space.

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:13.590
No matter what form it takes,
I will not be taken by surprise.

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:18.600
Love is infinite. Love is a spiral.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.350
Ah, busy. Ah, busy. So busy...

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.110
Hello, for the second time.

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:35.900
So, there is no need to be embarrassed regarding your relationship with Kanmuri.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:42.660
Starting now, we’ll begin the semifinals of
the newcomers’ battle for the B block!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.470
From the Southern Tokyo Branch: Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.670
All right, let’s do this!

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:51.300
Good luck, Kawachi!

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.170
Kawachi-san, good luck.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:57.680
From the Shinjuku Central Branch:
Kanmuri Shigeru.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:17:59.310
Step forward.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:04.680
I guess, there’s no impact
when you repeat it a second time.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.940
Ah, busy. Ah, busy. So busy.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.110
Good luck to you.

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:16.820
A true villain never appears as one, eh?

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:19.660
As long as I don’t know what they’re planning,

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.830
I’ll just ignore them.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:25.800
Ah, so cold...

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:30.330
But, if we don’t have at least that,
I wouldn’t get fired up, either.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:33.340
Oh well, try your best, please.

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:50.400
The basic ingredients have been prepared from our end.

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:54.980
Should you need anything other
than this, you may request it now.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.030
I don’t need anything else.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:59.740
I have this.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:02.410
What Kawachi is holding in his hand...

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:04.740
Without a doubt, it’s the hatsuga genmai yeast.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:09.250
I see... Matsushiro, eh?

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.790
But, Kawachi... you can’t...

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:15.500
No. Regardless of what anyone uses,
the results of this match are clear.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:22.640
If Kanmuri has really completed the yeast of dreams...

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.010
The Kaiyou yeast of fantasy...

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:39.080
This is your reward.

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:47.950
Semifinals for B block,

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:49.290
the theme is anything that you like.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:50.580
There’s no time limit.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.590
Begin!

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:01.090
The thing he has there...

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:02.800
Hatsuga genmai yeast?

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:18.020
Hatsuga genmai yeast plus...
solar gauntlets!

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:19.530
Put into operation!

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:26.450
Hatsuga genmai yeast
and solar gauntlets, eh?

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:29.700
It’s in the style of the old
gourmet battle shows, isn’t it?

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:33.040
But I quite like such people, Kawachi-san.

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.710
What’s with that dough?

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:39.550
It’s already risen so much...

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:41.520
How has he...?

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:44.050
Don’t tell me... he also...

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.140
Good luck, Kawachi!

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.560
Hang in there, Kawachi-san.

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.820
Why do I feel so uneasy?

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:08.740
That’s strange...

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:12.330
Kawachi-san’s dough is not rising at all.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.790
Even if it’s the fault of the hatsuga genmai yeast,

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:19.340
with solar gauntlets, it should have firmed up by now.

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:21.670
Don’t tell me...

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.090
The endo-proteases!

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:24.760
Here you go.

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:30.510
Earlier, the man in black brought in the ingredients.

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:32.730
Hydrolytic enzymes that can cleave protein.

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:35.440
If he mixed in the endo-proteases with the flour,

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.520
then the dough won’t become firm, no matter what.

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:39.110
What has she done...?

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:42.870
If we had just played out the match as normal, my win would be a 120% sure thing.

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:44.620
That woman!

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.960
You would go that far...?

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.210
Why...?

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:55.750
Why won’t it rise?

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.080
Did I mess up the quantity of water?

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.750
No, that can’t be.

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:03.050
Is it because the hatsuga genmai
yeast is too old to ferment?

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:06.380
No, Manager wouldn’t have
given me something like that.

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:10.050
Then, is it because my solar gauntlets are incomplete?

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:11.390
What in the world...?

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:13.060
What’s happening?

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:14.480
Do I just...

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:17.560
Do I just not have enough spirit?!

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:19.110
Mother,

00:22:19.110 --> 00:22:23.570
Kawachi-san seems to be having a
hard time at the newcomers’ battle.

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:26.320
However, do not worry.

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:27.570
I am just fine.

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:09.680
Why?

00:24:10.470 --> 00:24:12.630
Why won’t the dough firm up?

00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:16.140
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:18.680
The indomitable fighting spirit!!
Use adversity as a springboard to success!

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:24.730
Various proteases are
present in fruits such as pineapple.

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:26.070
They reduce the stomach’s workload,

00:24:26.070 --> 00:24:28.880
and help increase the rate of digestion and absorption.

00:24:28.880 --> 00:24:31.740
But, I don’t add pineapple to sweet and sour pork!

00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:33.360
Is that so?
